## Project context
Spring Boot 3.x Java 17 backend. BookMyShow ticketing system.
PostgreSQL + Redis + Kafka + Docker + AWS ECS.

## Code standards
- Always use constructor injection, never @Autowired field injection
- All service methods must be @Transactional where they write to DB
- Use @Slf4j for logging — never System.out.println
- Always add MDC.put("requestId", ...) at controller entry point
- Custom exceptions must extend RuntimeException, have a message
- DTOs must use records (Java 17) not plain classes

## What NOT to do
- Never hardcode connection strings or secrets
- Never catch generic Exception — always catch specific types
- Never return null from service methods — use Optional
- Never put business logic in controllers

## Testing
- Unit tests use Mockito, integration tests use @SpringBootTest
- Every service method needs at least one happy path + one exception test
